     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is about double the maximum labeled daily dose. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and for extended-release it is 2,000 mg/day. Metformin overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function. 1700 mg also isn't a standard tablet strength (500, 850, and 1000 mg are common).\n\nPlease confirm the intended regimen. For example:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum for IR)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg PO BID with meals** (3,400 mg/day), if you intend a dose above the usual maximum for a specific reason\n\nIf you confirm the dose as written, I can enter it, but I'd want you to verify it first. Please also tell me the indication, since that may affect the regimen."
      }
     ],
